{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00438",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 4.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Well, hello? Doctor? They told me to come straight in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.0,
      "end_seconds": 11.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Right, yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.53,
      "end_seconds": 15.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Um, so... wheezing. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.11,
      "end_seconds": 19.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.73,
      "end_seconds": 34.14,
      "duration_seconds": 12.41,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks now. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.78,
      "end_seconds": 38.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.65,
      "end_seconds": 58.28,
      "duration_seconds": 15.63,
      "text": "It's worse with cold air. Maybe a four out of ten on a bad day. I get some relief from the inhaler. I just want to get back to normal, really. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.9,
      "end_seconds": 62.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Right, anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.13,
      "end_seconds": 81.57,
      "duration_seconds": 18.44,
      "text": "So, it usually comes with a night-time cough. I've been using my blue inhaler more too, for five days. As for using my blue inhaler more, I'd say moderate. Yeah, I've also had shortness of breath on walking, since Friday. The night-time cough? That's been for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.39,
      "end_seconds": 85.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.07,
      "end_seconds": 88.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "It's, It's once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.46,
      "end_seconds": 91.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Right, what about weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.04,
      "end_seconds": 94.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Not at all, no weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.91,
      "end_seconds": 98.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Any chest pain, runny nose or leg swelling at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.84,
      "end_seconds": 107.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "I haven't had chest pain, runny nose or leg swelling, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.45,
      "end_seconds": 109.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Alright, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.85,
      "end_seconds": 112.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.82,
      "end_seconds": 116.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.65,
      "end_seconds": 118.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.17,
      "end_seconds": 122.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.82,
      "end_seconds": 130.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "It's Seretide inhaler, twice a day for my asthma. I take atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 130.73,
      "end_seconds": 135.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 10 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.42,
      "end_seconds": 140.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.83,
      "end_seconds": 144.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.01,
      "end_seconds": 149.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.03,
      "end_seconds": 165.52,
      "duration_seconds": 14.49,
      "text": "So, um, I have asthma, for about ten years. I did try to ignore it for a while. I have high cholesterol. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.94,
      "end_seconds": 168.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.77,
      "end_seconds": 184.73,
      "duration_seconds": 12.96,
      "text": "Okay, asthma, that's already on your record. Good to know. Yes, I can see the high cholesterol in your file as well. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.08,
      "end_seconds": 197.04,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.52,
      "end_seconds": 201.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.36,
      "end_seconds": 203.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.74,
      "end_seconds": 219.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 219.77,
      "end_seconds": 233.01,
      "duration_seconds": 13.24,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 21, weight 67 kilos, BMI works out to 23.7, saturation 94 percent, pressure 121 over 77, temperature is 36.7 degrees, height 168 centimetres, pulse is 104 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.26,
      "end_seconds": 251.39,
      "duration_seconds": 17.13,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.77,
      "end_seconds": 254.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.91,
      "end_seconds": 257.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.9,
      "end_seconds": 259.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.57,
      "end_seconds": 263.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.26,
      "end_seconds": 280.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "You're speaking in full sentences, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.39,
      "end_seconds": 283.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.84,
      "end_seconds": 296.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I can hear a widespread wheeze on both sides when you breathe out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.41,
      "end_seconds": 319.77,
      "duration_seconds": 18.36,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.06,
      "end_seconds": 323.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.19,
      "end_seconds": 338.03,
      "duration_seconds": 13.84,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: It fits best with an asthma flare-up. I can't rule out a chest infection yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had wheezing for about two weeks, and no weight loss or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.39,
      "end_seconds": 340.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 340.35,
      "end_seconds": 343.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "We've already done a peak flow reading this morning, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.66,
      "end_seconds": 360.86,
      "duration_seconds": 14.2,
      "text": "Perfect. We should do a chest X-ray for wheeze. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'd like to arrange breathing tests for asthma. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.52,
      "end_seconds": 363.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.43,
      "end_seconds": 387.17,
      "duration_seconds": 22.74,
      "text": "I'll start you on prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day, for five days. That should help with asthma flare-up. Let me watch you use the inhaler, a lot of people don't get the full dose. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.4,
      "end_seconds": 390.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Okay, you know, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.42,
      "end_seconds": 402.58,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the inhaler isn't helping or you can't speak in full sentences. That's the point to get seen urgently. Come back in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.9,
      "end_seconds": 410.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Sure, uh, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.06,
      "end_seconds": 417.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Let me check that I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.0,
      "end_seconds": 426.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "So, I take the prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.47,
      "end_seconds": 432.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Okay, yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.4,
      "end_seconds": 435.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 436.97,
      "end_seconds": 437.67,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}